  "ref": "DEU.22.2",
  "review_notes": [
    "The two 'if's belong to the single written 'im, which governs both members of the protasis; the second waw keeps only the 'or' written for it. This matches DEU.22.7, where lema'an takes both 'that's while its waw keeps 'and', and it is the reading rule 55 states for this verse by name.",
    "The competing reading, taken by the original pass, reads 'or if' as one coordinator-and-subordinator rendering of the waw under rule 55's pair sentence; that sentence governs a clause no written subordinator reaches, which is not this clause.",
    "Unchanged elsewhere: 'home' is read as the rendering of tokh rather than folded into 'bring', and the object marker takes the 'after' by which the English verb reaches its object under rule 16."
  ]
